      "event": "High Surf Advisory",
      "severity": "Minor",
      "urgency": "Expected",
      "certainty": "Likely",
      "headline": "High Surf Advisory issued November 10 at 3:16PM HST until November 12 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
      "description": "...HIGH SURF ADVISORY FOR NORTH AND WEST FACING SHORES OF NIIHAU\nKAUAI OAHU MOLOKAI AND NORTH FACING SHORES OF MAUI...\n\n.Surf heights will build through the day Wednesday, peak Wednesday\nnight and maintain advisory level heights Thursday.\n\n* WHAT....15 to 20 feet along north facing shores Wednesday and\nThursday, peaking 18 to 24 feet Wednesday night. 10 to 15 feet\nalong west facing shores Wednesday and Thursday, peaking 14 to\n18 feet Wednesday night.\n\n* WHERE...North and west facing shores of Niihau, Kauai, Oahu,\nMolokai and north facing shores of Maui.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 AM Wednesday to 6 PM HST Thursday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Moderate. Strong breaking waves and strong currents\nwill make swimming dangerous.",
      "instruction": "Heed all advice from ocean safety officials. When in doubt, don't\ngo out.",
      "areaDesc": "Niihau; Waianae Coast; Oahu North Shore; Maui Windward West; Kauai North; Molokai Windward; Molokai North; Molokai West; Maui Central Valley North; Windward Haleakala",
